                <pb facs="0078" n="28" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg28"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.51/266</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Special Representative</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">House</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1917-11-24T15:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 24,
                                1917, 3 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received November 25, 1.40
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have just told the French Prime Minister the substance of my cable this morning
                    concerning Russia and he earnestly indorses my opinion.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward
                            House</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
